# gtty-sessions with an ssh window and the job grid, restored in this
# gtty once it is untouched again (`close all`: a new shell nothing was
# typed into), with the stand-in ssh (the "remote machine" is this one). Run from a scratch folder (macOS, 1x display):
#   cc -o $REPO/test/fake-ssh/bin/ssh $REPO/test/fake-ssh/ssh.c
#   S=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p $S/home/alpha $S/home/beta $S/home/gamma
#   sed "s|@REPO@|$REPO|" $REPO/test/sessions-ssh.gt > $S/t.gt
#   cd $S && HOME=$S/home GTTY_SESSIONS=$S/sessions gtty --script t.gt
#   pkill -f "sshd: $USER@"     # the stand-in sshd processes it left
# Shots: 1 the snapshot's chip, 2 the manager (gamma in the grid column,
# the ssh tile with its host), 3 the untouched shell before the restore,
# 4 restored: the ssh command typed and run again (the restored shell
# has no stand-in on its PATH: the real ssh can't find `box`), gamma in
# the grid.
/s bash
/wait 1500
/type cd ~/alpha
/s bash
/wait 1500
/type export PATH=@REPO@/test/fake-ssh/bin:$PATH; clear
/wait 500
/type ssh -p 2222 me@box
/wait 1500
/type cd ~/beta
/wait 3500
/s bash
/wait 1500
/type cd ~/gamma
/wait 500
/click 1026 22
/wait 800
/menu snapshot
/wait 800
/shot ssh1-chip.bmp
/menu sessions
/wait 800
/target sessions
/shot ssh2-manager.bmp
/key escape
/target main
/wait 400
/close all
/wait 1800
/shot ssh3-untouched.bmp
/menu session-1
/wait 8000
/shot ssh4-restored.bmp
/quit
